geback calculations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the\n  idle-resource report for that project, then the console displays each\n  workbench's last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking), its owner, and its reserved resources.\n- Given a project containing pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n  stale pipeline-run report for that project, then the console lists\n  completed runs older than the configured age that retain artifacts,\n  sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- The staleness age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which\n  runs appear in the stale pipeline-run report.\n- Either report can be exported as CSV, and the exported file matches the\n  data displayed in the console for that report.\n- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines continue to operate without\n  modification while the reports consume their existing data (no code\n  changes land in those components; existing functionality is not regressed).\n- The console's build pipeline and tests are green with the new reporting\n  surface included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking — delivered by the idle-workbench report above.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n  run metadata — delivered by the stale pipeline-run report above.\n- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)**: CSV export of either report — bundled here because\n  it is an action on the same report surface and data the P1 reports build;\n  splitting it out would force a second pass over the same console surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35653,"output_tokens":0},"context_management