{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c3dee8dfd63d397","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers per-project idle-resource reporting in the RHOAI web\n34\tconsole. Cluster administrators get a single reporting surface per project\n35\tshowing (a) idle workbenches — last activity, owner, and reserved resources —\n36\tsourced from the notebook controller's existing activity tracking, and\n37\t(b) stale pipeline runs — completed runs older than a configurable age with\n38\tretained artifacts — sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. Either\n39\treport can be exported as CSV so admins can act on the data outside the\n40\tconsole. No new data collection is built: both source systems already track\n41\tthe needed metadata; this epic surfaces it.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- New per-project idle-resource reporting surface in the RHOAI web console\n46\t  (navigation and view), visible to cluster administrators.\n47\t- Idle-workbench report: per workbench in the project, show last activity\n48\t  (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and\n49\t  reserved resources.\n50\t- Stale pipeline-run report: list completed pipeline runs older than a\n51\t  configurable age that still retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow\n52\t  Pipelines run metadata.\n53\t- Configurable staleness age threshold for the pipeline-run report.\n54\t- CSV export of either report, matching the displayed data.\n55\t- Read-only consumption of the notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines\n56\t  data — no code changes in those components; they must keep working\n57\t  unchanged (validated as part of this epic's testing).\n58\t- Out of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources,\n59\t  cost/chargeback calculations.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the\n64\t  idle-resource report for that project, then the console displays each\n65\t  workbench's last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n66\t  tracking), its owner, and its reserved resources.\n67\t- Given a project containing pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n68\t  stale pipeline-run report for that project, then the console lists\n69\t  completed runs older than the configured age that retain artifacts,\n70\t  sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n71\t- The staleness age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which\n72\t  runs appear in the stale pipeline-run report.\n73\t- Either report can be exported as CSV, and the exported file matches the\n74\t  data displayed in the console for that report.\n75\t- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines continue to operate without\n76\t  modification while the reports consume their existing data (no code\n77\t  changes land in those components; existing functionality is not regressed).\n78\t- The console's build pipeline and tests are green with the new reporting\n79\t  surface included.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n84\t  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n85\t  tracking — delivered by the idle-workbench report above.\n86\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n87\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n88\t  run metadata — delivered by the stale pipeline-run report above.\n89\t- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)**: CSV export of either report — bundled here because\n90\t  it is an action on the same report surface and data the P1 reports build;\n91\t  splitting it out would force a second pass over the same console surface.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4436f4b0e98d549","agent_id":"a7b86efa383462704","session_id":"392b48d9-57ce-4faf-975b-753ba467ea17","uuid":"8a55e9f6-10ab-465d-9829-ea2f6e0fde92","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:08:39.205Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c3dee8dfd63d397","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
