{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be2bacd61b89c24d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9016 (Idle resource reporting in the web console)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage Note\n12\t\n13\tThe strategy has a single active component (the RHOAI web console / Dashboard,\n14\towned by one team) and no open questions, which would normally make it a\n15\tbelow-threshold candidate. However, HLR-4 calls for substantive documentation\n16\tauthoring (new doc topics explaining the reports and safe reclamation steps) —\n17\ta distinct work stream with its own review cycle — so the below-threshold\n18\tescape applies and the strategy received a full decomposition.\n19\t\n20\t## Step 1 — Strategy Structure\n21\t\n22\t- **Affected Components**: RHOAI web console (active — new report views),\n23\t  Notebook controller (passive — existing activity data consumed, no code\n24\t  changes), Kubeflow Pipelines (passive — existing run metadata consumed, no\n25\t  code changes).\n26\t- **Impacted Teams**: section absent from the strategy (health warning). Teams\n27\t  derived from architecture context.\n28\t- **High Level Requirements**: HLR-1 (P1, idle-workbench report), HLR-2 (P1,\n29\t  stale pipeline-run report), HLR-3 (P2, CSV export), HLR-4 (P2,\n30\t  documentation).\n31\t- **Dependencies**: section absent (health warning). No external dependencies\n32\t  stated; both data sources are in-platform components.\n33\t- **Acceptance Criteria**: no Given/When/Then section (health warning); epic\n34\t  ACs derived from the HLRs.\n35\t- **Non-Functional Requirements**: absent.\n36\t- **Staff Engineer Input**: absent — AI-generated content used as-is.\n37\t\n38\t## Component Graph\n39\t\n40\tCanonical component mappings (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n41\t\n42\t| Strategy name | Canonical component | Classification |\n43\t|---|---|---|\n44\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | Active (epic E001) |\n45\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Passive — validation folded into E001 ACs |\n46\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive — validation folded into E001 ACs |\n47\t\n48\tAll three components exist in `.context/architecture-context/`\n49\t(`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, `notebooks.md`,\n50\t`data-science-pipelines.md`) — no new-component onboarding chains are needed,\n51\tand the Dashboard is already Konflux-onboarded.\n52\t\n53\tPassive-component handling: the strategy states the data already exists\n54\t(\"the notebook controller already tracks last-activity timestamps, and\n55\tKubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata — the data exists; it is\n56\tjust not surfaced anywhere\"). Both passive components are consumed, not\n57\tmodified, by the console work owned by the same delivering effort, so their\n58\t\"keeps working\" validation is an acceptance criterion on E001 rather than a\n59\tseparate validation epic.\n60\t\n61\t## Investigation Epics\n62\t\n63\tNone. The strategy's Open Questions section is explicitly \"None\", and there\n64\tare no conditional ADRs or pending reviews. Remaining unknowns (exact console\n65\tAPI surface for notebook activity data, KFP metadata query shape, staleness\n66\tdefault) are implementation details the team resolves during work — captured\n67\tas ACs on E001, not Investigations.\n68\t\n69\t## Epic List\n70\t\n71\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n72\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Idle resource reporting documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n75\t\n76\tEpic boundary rationale: HLR-1 and HLR-2 are both P1 work on the same\n77\tcomponent (Dashboard), same team (RHOAI Dashboard), and the same logical\n78\tchange — the strategy's problem statement asks for \"a single report … showing\n79\tidle and stale resources per project\", i.e. one per-project reporting surface\n80\tin the console. Splitting the two reports into separate epics would have both\n81\tepics build the same report surface and CSV-export plumbing independently, so\n82\tthey stay in one epic. Documentation (HLR-4) is a separate work-product type\n83\t(docs content authoring) and a separate component, so it is its own\n84\t`docs-authoring` epic.\n85\t\n86\t## Dependency DAG\n87\t\n88\t```mermaid\n89\tgraph TD\n90\t    E001[\"RHAISTRAT-9016-E001: Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\"] --> E002[\"RHAISTRAT-9016-E002: Idle resource reporting documentation\"]\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t## DAG Justification\n94\t\n95\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n96\t|------|------|-----------|\n97\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation describes what was built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy (here, E001). Per the docs-authoring priority exception, this edge does not push E002's P2 priority onto E001. |\n98\t\n99\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n100\t\n101\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n102\t|-----|----------|------|-------|\n103\t| HLR-1 | P1 | E001 | Idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook controller activity tracking. |\n104\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E001 | Stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. |\n105\t| HLR-3 | P2 | E001 | **(bundled)** CSV export of either report shares the reports' UI surface and data — it is an action on the same tables the P1 work builds, not a separately schedulable feature; splitting it would force a second pass over the same surface. |\n106\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E002 | Documentation of the reports and safe reclamation steps. |\n107\t\n108\tFull coverage: all four HLRs map to at least one epic; no orphaned\n109\trequirements. No priority inversion: E001 carries P1 (highest priority of its\n110\tmapped HLRs, with HLR-3 bundled); E002 is P2 via the docs-authoring exception\n111\t(strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2).\n112\t\n113\t## Health Warnings\n114\t\n115\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n116\t  table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no Non-Functional\n117\t  Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs and problem statement;\n118\t  epic ACs are derived from HLR wording. Team assignments were derived from\n119\t  architecture context (`RHOAI Dashboard` per dashboard.md); the Documentation\n120\t  component has no architecture-context file, so `RHOAI Documentation` is an\n121\t  assumption — verify with the doc team before scheduling.\n122\t- **Epic kept above the ~2-week guideline (E001)**: estimated ~2–3 weeks\n123\t  (two backend data integrations — notebook-controller activity data and KFP\n124\t  run metadata — plus the shared per-project report surface and CSV export).\n125\t  A split by report would duplicate the shared reporting surface and export\n126\t  plumbing and force a second pass over the same console area. **Conditional\n127\t  re-split trigger**: re-split E001 by report (idle-workbench vs.\n128\t  stale pipeline-run) if either backend data integration exceeds ~1.5 weeks\n129\t  of estimated effort, or if implementation reveals the two reports ship on\n130\t  separate console pages/surfaces rather than one reporting surface.\n131\t- **Scope trap (informational)**: the reports must surface \"reserved\n132\t  resources\" for workbenches — the strategy does not define which reservations\n133\t  count (CPU/memory requests, PVCs). This is an implementation-detail decision\n134\t  for the Dashboard team, captured as an AC on E001, not an Investigation.\n135\t- **Out-of-scope boundary is clean**: automated reclamation/deletion and\n136\t  cost/chargeback are explicitly out of scope; no epic touches them, and the\n137\t  documentation epic's \"safe reclamation steps\" cover manual reclamation only.\n138\t\n139\t## Tiered Delivery\n140\t\n141\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing. Both data\n142\tsources are in-platform, GA components.\n143\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5b36af7a6fa2bfa","agent_id":"ab7727edd39ea9b4b","session_id":"392b48d9-57ce-4faf-975b-753ba467ea17","uuid":"7c56826b-c5f2-4d3f-ac5f-1b115c5cc463","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:10:52.398Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be2bacd61b89c24d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
