t.\n52\t- Stale pipeline-run report documentation: what \"stale\" means (completed runs\n53\t  older than the configured age with retained artifacts), how to configure\n54\t  the age threshold, and the data source (Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n55\t- How to export either report as CSV.\n56\t- Safe reclamation steps: manual, administrator-controlled steps for\n57\t  reclaiming capacity from idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs\n58\t  (including artifact cleanup considerations), consistent with the strategy's\n59\t  out-of-scope boundary — automated reclamation and cost/chargeback are not\n60\t  documented as features.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Published documentation explains both reports, the fields each displays,\n65\t  and where in the console to find them.\n66\t- Published documentation explains the configurable staleness age for the\n67\t  stale pipeline-run report and how to change it.\n68\t- Published documentation explains how to export either report as CSV.\n69\t- Published documentation includes safe reclamation steps covering both idle\n70\t  workbenches and stale pipeline runs, clearly scoped to manual reclamation.\n71\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented console\n72\t  reports so every described field, control, and step matches the shipped\n73\t  behavior.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation\n78\t  steps — delivered by the content outline above.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5b36af7a6fa2bfa","agent_id":"ab7727edd39ea9b4b","session_id":"392b48d9-57ce-4faf-975b-753ba467ea17","uuid":"b2d33449-033f-4499-b34f-198b74cb8f85","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:10:57.461Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adace73fff6e62df","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
